From 6c01b134a1d70445d28de9e7ac0e67f928e8291b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SteveDeFacto <5148995+SteveDeFacto@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 02:08:38 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 19/28] Integrate the kernel lock, final witness helper and
 optional S3 archive into the verifier runtime

The runtime now holds its stateDir with root's parent-owned kernel flock (network/runtime-lock.mjs,
794d2ff3): the PID-file takeLock is deleted, runtime.lock stays a persistent empty file that is never
unlinked, the release (registered before any further await) closes the descriptor, a nonempty
legacy lock is refused unchanged, and the stateDir must be private (0700, our uid). util-linux flock
and, with an archive, curl with --aws-sigv4 are reviewed absolute paths (hostTools), preflighted.

Config format enclave-rpc-runtime/v2 (v1 refused):
  * witnessCache must be null: a local cache would allocate NVMe, and every such cache must be a
    root-approved reservation in the central budget (enclave-rpc-nvme-cache-budget/v2, 250 GB hard
    aggregate), whose v2 kinds reserve only preallocated files; no competing quota is invented;
  * witnessArchive (optional): P/E's S3 archive tier (s3-witness-cache.mjs) behind the gateway, read
    only after every proof source failed, re-verified, writes opt-in; never contacted to start;
    credentials from a 0600 file of the runtime user; scratch under <stateDir>/tmp (<= 2 x 4 MiB);
  * only the final helper is accepted: witness-check 4fe0cd3b (Helios ef320298, adds the block op);
    the aca81764 helpers fab2f1ce/a3377048 are dropped. Helios cc962e2b and the listener builds stay.
Shutdown closes gateway, archive, relay, root store and helper in that order. Status and docs say
what the corrected audit supports: no usable maintained peer-proof source is established for this
runtime (snap/2 implemented, default off, no Base flag, peer availability unknown); fresh state needs
a configured, reachable proof source.

Composed-process tests: cold start with every proof source and the archive down; admin platform-policy
ban through the runtime; retained clients closed after success and deadline; the archive serving
verified history with every source down, never fresh state, and refusing once it fails too; a second
runtime on a live stateDir refused; two simultaneous cold starts with one owner; a legacy lock
refused unchanged; a SIGKILLed runtime whose orphaned Helios holds no lock descriptor, then a clean
restart; the lock file persisting and reacquirable after shutdown. build-binaries.sh pins Helios
ef320298 and gains a no-compile `check` mode for the input closure.
